{"title":"2024 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Given_more_advanced_knowledge)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Given more advanced knowledge)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Basic_Mod_Almost_same_as_sol_one)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Basic Mod Almost same as sol one)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#🎥✨_Video_Solution_by_Scholars_Foundation_➡️_(Easy-to-Understand_💡✔️)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">🎥✨ Video Solution by Scholars Foundation ➡️ (Easy-to-Understand 💡✔️)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_Pi_Academy_(Fast_and_Easy_⚡🚀)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by Pi Academy (Fast and Easy ⚡🚀)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/6/3d6101280c26c909edc6ab372d640be60a5e34ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7^{2024}+7^{2025}+7^{2026}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37eef8b202a1cae059bfd99504f4006fe4c0104.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 0 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 1 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 7 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 11 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"373\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can factor the expression as\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05f12ad7ed22ebbea9c9e4437c5ba95e02476353.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[7^{2024} (1 + 7 + 7^2) = 7^{2024} (57).\\]\" width=\"225\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/f/b5fe0b1d5852d2b41bcacf454d7facda14473c92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$57=19\\cdot3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />, this expression is actually divisible by 19. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a054d23afde92b8d87cebc50411cc3aeb0d3b401.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If you failed to realize that the expression can be factored, you might also apply modular arithmetic to solve the problem.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cd010871af4134280648fd3efb64f8563cd677e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7^3\\equiv1\\pmod{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"21\" />, the powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> repeat every three terms:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/4/c241c520618add32d93f1ceec343a869bff401e0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[7^1\\equiv7\\pmod{19}\\]\" width=\"138\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/8/7884bae9a7c83119054fe26642be6f54fa5d3558.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[7^2\\equiv11\\pmod{19}\\]\" width=\"147\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96a87b5ffd4ca057d6e94eef31d6fb7de25d590c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[7^3\\equiv1\\pmod{19}\\]\" width=\"138\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>The fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce029dc28cb41483452be5cf2232153b458f7154.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2024\\equiv2\\pmod3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/2/9428bfaa4c4d5a706add5f8aa1690326890bb070.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025\\equiv0\\pmod3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/f/6afeab4b686525705ba10ff4b5e7ddc34035d26a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026\\equiv1\\pmod3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" /> implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/8/5a87916c4457fdcfc305ae76e7b330b94520ae7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7^{2024}+7^{2025}+7^{2026}\\equiv11+1+7\\equiv19 \\equiv0\\pmod{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"418\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Bloggish\" title=\"User:Bloggish\">Bloggish</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We start the same as solution 2, and find that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/4/c241c520618add32d93f1ceec343a869bff401e0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[7^1\\equiv7\\pmod{19}\\]\" width=\"138\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/8/7884bae9a7c83119054fe26642be6f54fa5d3558.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[7^2\\equiv11\\pmod{19}\\]\" width=\"147\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96a87b5ffd4ca057d6e94eef31d6fb7de25d590c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[7^3\\equiv1\\pmod{19}\\]\" width=\"138\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>We know that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e5711c8d31d3bc3119aba377c9bda0f9dfb14e4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2024$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e513adf78ee28ac3403e90a42259bc55f59e2d8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, because there are three terms, we can just add them up. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d663d16ec77d078571eebf36a412583a3bc7fdd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 7 + 11 = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"125\" height=\"15\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Given_more_advanced_knowledge.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Given_more_advanced_knowledge)\">Solution 4 (Given more advanced knowledge)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Given more advanced knowledge)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By Fermat's Little Theorem (FLT), we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/7/52712c18689479933820da01da7f52a9a365ba8b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[7^{18}\\equiv1\\pmod{19}\\]\" width=\"145\" height=\"20\" /> Then its order must divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Trying simple values we try and succeed: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96a87b5ffd4ca057d6e94eef31d6fb7de25d590c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[7^3\\equiv1\\pmod{19}\\]\" width=\"138\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\nSo the expression is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/d/dbd89f3202717cf66a2d13ac86867403400e1001.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+7+49\\pmod{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"164\" height=\"20\" />, which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a054d23afde92b8d87cebc50411cc3aeb0d3b401.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" /> when divided by 19.\n</p><p><br />\n~xHypotenuse\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Basic_Mod_Almost_same_as_sol_one.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Basic_Mod_Almost_same_as_sol_one)\">Solution 5 (Basic Mod Almost same as sol one)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Basic Mod Almost same as sol one)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have \\begin{align*}7^{2024} \\cdot (1+7+49) &amp;\\equiv 0 \\pmod{19}\\\\ 57 &amp;\\equiv 0 \\pmod{19},\\end{align*} so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a054d23afde92b8d87cebc50411cc3aeb0d3b401.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" />. \n</p><p>~Cheerfulfrog\n</p><p>~ better latex by SuperVince1\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\".F0.9F.8E.A5.E2.9C.A8_Video_Solution_by_Scholars_Foundation_.E2.9E.A1.EF.B8.8F_.28Easy-to-Understand_.F0.9F.92.A1.E2.9C.94.EF.B8.8F.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"🎥✨_Video_Solution_by_Scholars_Foundation_➡️_(Easy-to-Understand_💡✔️)\">🎥✨ Video Solution by Scholars Foundation ➡️ (Easy-to-Understand 💡✔️)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: 🎥✨ Video Solution by Scholars Foundation ➡️ (Easy-to-Understand 💡✔️)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/T_QESWAKUUk?si=5euBbKNMaYBROuTV&amp;t=100\">https://youtu.be/T_QESWAKUUk?si=5euBbKNMaYBROuTV&amp;t=100</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Pi_Academy_.28Fast_and_Easy_.E2.9A.A1.F0.9F.9A.80.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Pi_Academy_(Fast_and_Easy_⚡🚀)\">Video Solution 1 by Pi Academy (Fast and Easy ⚡🚀)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by Pi Academy (Fast and Easy ⚡🚀)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/QLziG_2e7CY?feature=shared\">https://youtu.be/QLziG_2e7CY?feature=shared</a>\n</p><p>~ Pi Academy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=24EZaeAThuE\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=24EZaeAThuE</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ZaHv4UkXcbs?t=208\">https://youtu.be/ZaHv4UkXcbs?t=208</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B\" title=\"2024 AMC 10B\">2024 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2024 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2024 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems